{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry you missed the Q4 planning invite. I looked into it: the invite isn't stuck in your spam quarantine, and your mailbox and account both look fine. Here are a few things that will help find it: 1) Open Outlook on the web and check your calendar and inbox there for the invite. Does it show up there even if it doesn't in the desktop app? 2) Does anyone, such as an assistant or teammate, manage your calendar for you? If so, the invite may have gone only to them. 3) Who organized the meeting? Do you normally get emails and invites from that person, or do their messages never seem to reach you? The quickest fix is usually to ask the organizer to send the invite to you again. Please reply with your answers and let us know if the resent invite still doesn't arrive.",
  "internal_note": "I followed KB-012. User: Sofia Rossi (id 7), Marketing. Her account is active and her mailbox is 27.9% full, so it isn't a quota problem. The spam quarantine is empty, so there is nothing to release. My tools can't check delegate settings or compare web vs desktop Outlook, so I asked her about both and asked her to have the organizer resend the invite (KB-012 Fix step 4). If invites from one specific internal organizer never arrive, escalate to Tier 2 as a possible mail rule or transport issue under KB-012. If only the desktop app is missing it, follow the KB-009 sync steps.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-012"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
